Fixes, most-cited first, with the lenses that asked:

1. Chat leaders must not cross the thread. All eight lenses asked (feedback (3), soul, style (2), system (1), interaction (2), type, usability (4), skeptic (1)). Answered by drawing the sequence diagram in each message's own row, as system asked in tour round 1 ('a gutter beside the thread, at the thread's line pitch'). Arrows become links (interaction, r1).
2. 'This page' lit amber, with a word beside every lamp and a one-line caution under the Status head. Asked by system (2), interaction (1), usability (1) and skeptic (5).
3. The navy sheets: sheet toward green-black and grid at half alpha. Asked by feedback (2), soul (relit fix), skeptic (3) and soul's Relit note.
4. Phosphor back. Asked by soul, style (1, 5), feedback (4) and skeptic (7):
   - Relit's tubes (t2-figure-mut, tour/t2-b/variants/t2-figure-mut/sheet.css E12-E17 blocks);
   - Gauged's round tube on Plans (T2-42, tour/t2-b/variants/t2-figure-graft);
   - the spend tube moved into the first screen;
   - E1 on 'plan';
   - lamps, not tubes, under 1.2rem.
5. Home: one NOW line (feedback 1); one lit mark per figure (style 3, system 3); Next up said once (skeptic 4); the rail started at the head (interaction 4).
6. Plans: week ranges level with their stops (feedback 5, system 5), and empty weeks folded behind a break mark (interaction 3, usability 5, style 1, skeptic 6; Gauged's break mark).
7. 'All 4 · 2 late' as one head link (system 6, usability 6).
8. Restaurant to clay #c79071 (skeptic 2).
9. Type:
   - a 22px Home plate step;
   - the Plans hairline stopped at 46rem;
   - a fixed due column with Edit on its line;
   - the chat date in mono rail style (all from type);
   - 14px sentence-case eyebrows (interaction 4);
   - rail dates in a muted sky ink (style 4).
10. To do's Show as segmented one-press keys (usability 3).
11. '#n' ids dropped from Home (usability 7).
12. Sign-in in the main column (usability 8).

Small borrowing: E10 landing flash, from the kit, so the jump links visibly land.

Four features, each rebuilt in the manual's ink, line and phosphor:

1. L076, 'Her screen wired to whoever has spoken' (GEM). From r12-mut-3 Slate Flight Console (round 12, 6.96, #9 of 17). Files: rounds/r12/variants/r12-mut-3/templates/chat.html ~21-45 and sheet.css ~879-889 (.tile-loop, .wire, .node, .node-them, .who-n, .her, .her-case). It becomes Fig. 0 on Home's greeting glass, replacing the Next up radar tube, and Chat's lane heads. Its own caveats are answered: the last speaker's node is lit and named, and the figure is labelled. Its ledger entry says it suits figure as 'the Chat section's figure drawn from its own data'.
2. L088, 'People as monogram initials, no tiles' (GEM). From r13-wmut-1 Folio Switchboard (round 13, 6.88, #9 of 17). Files: rounds/r13/variants/r13-wmut-1/sheet.css .initial/.roster 1234-1244, .said-them .avatar 1649, .kids-cell .initial 1676, .person-cell .avatar 2135; templates/chat.html, family.html. Rebuilt in Plex Sans Condensed 300, bone and heather (no Fraunces, no pink), in Fig. 0, Chat's lanes, the To do tally and Family.
3. L112, 'Glow where you land from a link' (GEM). From r11-wild-4 Videotex Sommaire (round 11, 5.98, #14 of 17). File: rounds/r11/variants/r11-wild-4/sheet.css line 1076 and 1835-1841. Rebuilt as the lineage rule 'every figure mark is a link to its row, and the row lights on landing'. It answers the old interaction note that the chat's arrows and the wiring's ports were pictures, not links, and gives the afterglow a job.
4. L042, 'Setup cut to one line' (GEM). From r12-wild-4 Single Quote (round 12, 6.59, #11 of 17). Files: rounds/r12/variants/r12-wild-4/sheet.css ~1118-1137 and templates/home.html. Rebuilt as the manual's hung Caution note. It answers usability's round-2 fix (2), 'Finish setting up takes four rows'.

The lineage's fixes also applied here:
- the chat stub, not leaders (all eight lenses);
- the amber 'This page' with words beside the lamps (system, interaction, usability, skeptic);
- green-black sheets (feedback, soul, skeptic);
- the round tubes for Plans and spend, and E1 on the lit word (soul, style, skeptic);
- folded empty weeks and centred week ranges (interaction, usability, feedback, system);
- clay restaurants (skeptic);
- a 22px plate step (type);
- segmented Show keys (usability);
- no '#n' ids on Home (usability).

The free universal fixes (44px targets, sentence case, late in words, tabular figures, underlined links, one control per filter) are taken.
